The encoder libjpeg: JPEG pictures by the libjpeg API, with the library ffmpeg is
linked with (mozjpeg of az here; libjpeg-turbo and jpegli have the same API), for
the formats of the screenshots of the video sites by ffmpeg alone, without
ImageMagick (aZ, 25.11.2026 17:39: «пиши обёртку»).

A site makes a screenshot with ffmpeg (mjpeg) and then each format of it
(320x180, 640x360...) with ImageMagick: two lossy steps, two programs that read
what users upload. The encoder mjpeg of FFmpeg takes only a whole -q:v (1, 2, 3...:
15-30% of bytes a step) and has neither trellis quantisation nor optimised scans.
libjpeg writes a JPEG as ImageMagick does, from RGB: the library converts it to
YCbCr (JFIF: BT.601, full range) and subsamples the chroma itself, and -quality
means what it means to ImageMagick and cjpeg. The conversion of a video to RGB is
done by libswscale before it, with the colour matrix of the video, so a BT.709 video
keeps its colours (the screenshot of the sites puts BT.709 YCbCr into the JPEG as it
is, read everywhere as BT.601).

Options: -quality 0-100 (else -q:v, else 75); -sampling 420|422|444 (default 420);
-dct islow|ifast|float (default islow, the accurate DCT); -progressive -1|0|1 (as
the library: mozjpeg progressive with optimised scans); -optimize 0|1 (Huffman
tables, default 1); -comment (a COM marker). The aspect ratio of a pixel goes into
the JFIF header, as the mjpeg encoder writes it. Errors of the library go to the log
(setjmp/longjmp), the frame fails with AVERROR_EXTERNAL; 1x1, odd sizes, grey and
65500 pixels a side work, larger is refused.

Checked against ImageMagick 7.1.2-36 and cjpeg of mozjpeg 4.1.5 built with the
same flags, from the same RGB picture: the same bytes at -quality 50 to 100 as
magick -strip -define jpeg:dct-method=islow -sampling-factor 2x2 -quality Q and as
cjpeg -sample 2x2 -quality Q, and as magick -strip -quality Q (which takes the fast
DCT up to quality 90 and 4:4:4 from 90 when it does not read a JPEG) with -dct ifast
up to 90 and -sampling 444 from 90. A mozjpeg built with other compiler flags can
round one 8x8 block differently (its trellis is floating point).

